# Architecture

Workspaces: `apps/*`, `packages/*`, `server`, `database`, `e2e`.

## Layers

Apps → Express routes/controllers → services → `@npha/scoring-engine` / `@npha/pdf-engine` + Prisma (`@npha/database`).

See `docs/architecture/OVERVIEW.md`.

## Packages

| Package | Path | Boundary |
|---------|------|----------|
| `@npha/shared` | `packages/shared` | Types, Zod schemas, permissions, socket rooms — **SSoT** |
| `@npha/ui` | `packages/ui` | Shared React UI + `globals.css` tokens |
| `@npha/utils` | `packages/utils` | Pure helpers (CSV, names, QR payload) |
| `@npha/scoring-engine` | `packages/scoring-engine` | Pure scoring — **no** Express/Prisma/React |
| `@npha/pdf-engine` | `packages/pdf-engine` | PDF generation — framework-agnostic |
| `@npha/database` | `database` | Prisma schema, migrations, seed, client |

## Integration

- Vite apps proxy `/api` → `http://localhost:4000`.
- Clients call `/api/v1/...` via each app’s `src/lib/api.ts`.
- Real-time: Socket.IO rooms from `@npha/shared` `SOCKET_ROOMS` (`server/src/socket/index.ts`).

## Rules

- Do not duplicate API types or Zod schemas inside apps — extend `@npha/shared`.
- Do not put Prisma or HTTP inside scoring/pdf engines.
- Keep controllers thin; business logic lives in `server/src/services/`.
- User-facing branding/org/sponsor/country data must come from configuration or DB — never hardcoded product copy.
